    "q-6684": {
      "dom_id": "step-q6684",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Is the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$, for $x\\ne 0$, even, odd, or neither?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that\n\n- a function is even if $f(-x)=f(x)$ for all $x,$ while\n\n- a function is odd if $f(-x)=-f(x)$ for all $x.$\n\nComputing $f(-x)$ for the given function and comparing it to $f(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =\\frac{1}{(-x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=f(x),$ the function is even.\n\nLastly, we compute $-f(x)$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-f(x) & =-(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)\\ne -f(x),$ the function is not odd.\n\nTherefore, the function is only even.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
