    "q-36592": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36592",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The table below defines the function $f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is an even function, find the value of $a+b.$\n\n| **$x$** | $-23$ | $-15$ | $-7$ | $7$ | $15$ | $23$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $a+5$ | $-\\sqrt{2}$ | $b+1$ | $4$ | $-\\sqrt{2}$ | $6$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is an even function, we must have that $f(-x)=f(x).$ \n\nUsing the fact that $f(-23)=f(23),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-23) & =f(23) \\\\ a+5 & =6 \\\\ a & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $f(-7)=f(7),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-7) & =f(7) \\\\ b+1 & =4 \\\\ b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b=1+3=4.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
