    "q-110665": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110665",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The table below defines the function $f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is an even function, find the value of $a+b.$\n\n| **$x$** | $-90$ | $-65$ | $-40$ | $40$ | $65$ | $90$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $16$ | $b-2$ | $-8$ | $-8$ | $-1$ | $a+6$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is an even function, we must have that $f(-x)=f(x).$ \n\nUsing the fact that $f(-90)=f(90),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-90) & =f(90) \\\\ 16 & =a+6 \\\\ a & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $f(-65)=f(65),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-65) & =f(65) \\\\ b-2 & =-1 \\\\ b & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\na+b=10+1=11.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
